import ../../../ui/scene_baking.dl
import ../../../ui/scene_normals.dl
import ../../../ui/scene_surfaces.dl

to check baked number {a number:actual} equals {a number:expected}:
    require condition ((the absolute value of (actual - expected)) < 0.00001) reporting "A baked scene mesh component changed."

require condition ((the size of linear UI paint) = 12) reporting "Mesh colors must use a portable float32 RGB stream."
require condition ((the size of UI mesh vertex) = 32) reporting "A color stream changed the existing position/normal/UV layout."
set mesh to a UI box mesh with 1 by 1 by 1 segments
require condition ((the length of mesh's colors) = (the length of mesh's vertices)) reporting "A mesh has incomplete vertex colors."
for each color in mesh's colors:
    check baked number (color's red) equals 1.0
    check baked number (color's green) equals 1.0
    check baked number (color's blue) equals 1.0
set red to linear UI ink from (UI ink 255 0 0)
set gray to linear UI ink from (UI ink 128 128 128)
check baked number (gray's red) equals 0.21586050011389926
check baked number (gray's green) equals (gray's red)
set batch to a UI mesh builder
set identity to a UI scene transform from (an identity graphics matrix)
append UI mesh mesh through identity tinted red to batch
set shifted to a UI scene transform from (a graphics translation by x 3.0 y 0.0 z 0.0)
append UI mesh mesh through shifted tinted gray to batch
set baked to a completed UI mesh from batch
require condition (((the length of baked's vertices) = 48) and ((the length of baked's indices) = 72)) reporting "Mesh baking changed indexed geometry or repeated a draw's vertices."
require condition ((the length of baked's colors) = 48) reporting "Mesh baking lost its separate color stream."
check baked number (baked's bounds' minimum's x) equals -0.5
check baked number (baked's bounds' maximum's x) equals 3.5
check baked number ((the item at 0 in baked's colors)'s red) equals 1.0
check baked number ((the item at 0 in baked's colors)'s blue) equals 0.0
check baked number ((the item at 24 in baked's colors)'s green) equals (gray's green)
set again to a UI mesh builder
append UI mesh baked through identity tinted (linear UI ink red 0.5 green 1.0 blue 1.0) to again
set copy to a completed UI mesh from again
check baked number ((the item at 0 in copy's colors)'s red) equals 0.5
check baked number ((the item at 24 in copy's colors)'s red) equals (gray's red * 0.5)
check baked number ((the item at 0 in baked's colors)'s red) equals 1.0

# Mirrored baking fixes triangle winding while preserving transformed normals.
set batch to a UI mesh builder
set mirrored to a UI scene transform from (a graphics scale by x -2.0 y 3.0 z 4.0)
append UI mesh mesh through mirrored tinted gray to batch
set baked to a completed UI mesh from batch
set index to 0
loop while index < the length of baked's indices:
    set first to the item at (the item at index in baked's indices) in baked's vertices
    set second to the item at (the item at (index + 1) in baked's indices) in baked's vertices
    set third to the item at (the item at (index + 2) in baked's indices) in baked's vertices
    set edge to (the UI mesh position of second) - (the UI mesh position of first)
    set side to (the UI mesh position of third) - (the UI mesh position of first)
    require condition ((the dot product of (the cross product of edge and side) and (the UI mesh normal of first)) > 0.0) reporting "Mirrored baking left an inward-facing triangle."
    set index to index + 3

# Shared normals are area-weighted and accumulated into float32 vertex storage.
set vertices to an empty list of UI mesh vertex
set indices to an empty list of a 32 bit unsigned integer
set zero to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
for each point in [(a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0), (a new vector with x 2.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0), (a new vector with x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0), (a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0), (a new vector with x 9.0, y 9.0 and z 9.0)]:
    append UI mesh vertex at point normal zero uv 0.0 0.0 to vertices
append UI mesh triangle 0 1 2 to indices
append UI mesh triangle 0 3 1 to indices
append UI mesh triangle 0 0 0 to indices
recalculate UI mesh normals in vertices using indices
set normal to the UI mesh normal of (the item at 0 in vertices)
check baked number (normal's x) equals 0.0
check baked number (normal's y) equals (1.0 / the square root of 2.0)
check baked number (normal's z) equals (normal's y)
check baked number (the length of (the UI mesh normal of (the item at 4 in vertices))) equals 0.0
set custom to a UI scene mesh taking vertices vertices and indices indices
free vertices
free indices
set batch to a UI mesh builder
append UI mesh custom through identity tinted gray to batch
set custom to a completed UI mesh from batch
check baked number (the length of (the UI mesh normal of (the item at 4 in custom's vertices))) equals 0.0
set batch to a UI mesh builder
set empty to a completed UI mesh from batch
require condition (((the length of empty's vertices) = 0) and ((the length of empty's colors) = 0)) reporting "An empty mesh batch did not remain a valid owning value."
print line "Scene meshes batch indexed geometry with linear vertex colors, transformed normals, mirrored winding and area-weighted normal generation."
